     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the FDA maximum of 2,550 mg/day, and the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided (for example, 850 mg twice daily)\n\nIf you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I can enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it now."
      }
     ],
